From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:05:05 +0200
Subject: [parser] Validate non-pattern sub-expressions in patterns and arrow
 heads

In `ParsePossibleDestructuringSubPattern`, when a sub-pattern is a
`Property` (`[{a = 42}.b] = []`), `scope->ValidateExpression()` was
called so inner expression errors were reported. However, when the
sub-pattern was any other non-pattern expression (`[{a = 42}.f()] = []`,
`[!{a = 42}] = []`, `[{a = 42} + 1] = []`, `[{a = 42}?.b] = []`),
`ValidateExpression()` was not called, causing outer pattern validation
to clear the inner expression error and report `Invalid destructuring
assignment target` instead.

Similarly, `ClassifyArrowParameter` did not call `ValidateExpression()`
when an arrow parameter was neither an identifier, pattern, nor
assignment (`({a = 42}.b) => {}`, `({a = 42} + 1) => {}`).

Validate inner expression errors via `AccumulationScope::ValidateExpression()`
in both places before recording the pattern or declaration error.

